    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "98118261"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Reasoning**:\n",
        "First, I'll import the necessary metrics from `sklearn.metrics` and define a helper function `communities_to_labels` to convert community sets into node label lists suitable for NMI and ARI calculations. This is crucial as `sklearn`'s metrics expect a flat list of labels for each node.\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "id": "98118261"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "43d4ad12",
        "outputId": "057fbdb5-dbb5-4b9b-9779-4c26d907465f"
      },
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.metrics import normalized_mutual_info_score, adjusted_rand_score\n",
        "\n",
        "def communities_to_labels(communities, num_nodes):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Converts a list of community sets into a list of node labels.\n",
        "    Each node is assigned the ID of its community. If a node belongs to multiple communities,\n",
        "    it will be assigned to one of them (e.g., the first one encountered). If a node is not\n",
        "    in any community, it gets a special label (e.g., -1).\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    labels = [-1] * num_nodes  # Initialize with a default label for unassigned nodes\n",
        "    community_id_counter = 0\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Create a mapping from node to its community ID\n",
        "    # If a node is in multiple communities, we'll just assign it the ID of the first one we see.\n",
        "    # For ground truth and non-overlapping algorithms, each node should belong to exactly one.\n",
        "    node_to_community_map = {}\n",
        "    for comm_id, community_set in enumerate(communities):\n",
        "        for node in community_set:\n",
        "            # If a node is already assigned, this would mean it's in overlapping communities.\n",
        "            # For NMI/ARI, each node needs a single ground truth label.\n",
        "            # We'll assign the first community ID it's found in.\n",
        "            if node not in node_to_community_map:\n",
        "                node_to_community_map[node] = comm_id\n",
        "\n",
        "    for node_idx in range(num_nodes):\n",
        "        if node_idx in node_to_community_map:\n",
        "            labels[node_idx] = node_to_community_map[node_idx]\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Ensure all nodes are covered. If any node is still -1, assign a unique new community ID.\n",
        "    # This scenario should ideally not happen for ground truth or partitions from LPA/Louvain.\n",
        "    for node_idx in range(num_nodes):\n",
        "        if labels[node_idx] == -1:\n",
        "            # Assign a new unique ID for nodes not in any detected community\n",
        "            labels[node_idx] = community_id_counter + len(communities) # offset to avoid clash with existing community IDs\n",
        "            community_id_counter += 1\n",
        "\n",
        "    return labels\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Imported NMI/ARI functions and defined communities_to_labels utility function.\")"
      ],
      "id": "43d4ad12",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Imported NMI/ARI functions and defined communities_to_labels utility function.\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
