        "\n",
        "### Q&A\n",
        "The subtask implicitly asks for an interpretation of node roles based on their positions in the z-P scatter plot.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Interpretation of Node Roles:**\n",
        "Nodes are categorized into roles based on their within-module z-score (zᵢ) and participation coefficient (Pᵢ).\n",
        "*   **Peripheral nodes (P \\$\\le\\$ 0.6, z \\$\\leq\\$ 2.5):** These nodes have most of their connections within their own community and are not highly connected within their community. They primarily participate in activities internal to their module.\n",
        "*   **Non-hub connector nodes (P $>$ 0.6, z $\\leq$ 2.5):** These nodes have connections distributed across different communities but are not highly connected within their own community. They act as bridges between communities without being central to any single one.\n",
        "*   **Non-hub kinless nodes (P $\\leq$ 0.6, z $>$ 2.5):** These nodes are highly connected within their own community but have few connections to other communities. They are central to their module's function but do not significantly link to other modules.\n",
        "*   **Connector hubs (P $>$ 0.6, z $>$ 2.5):** These nodes are highly connected both within their own community and across different communities. They are crucial for both internal community cohesion and inter-community communication, acting as central points for the overall network structure.\n",
        "\n",
        "The scatter plot visually delineates these regions using thresholds of P = 0.6 and z = 2.5.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Data Analysis Key Findings\n",
