        "*   Thresholds of P = 0.6 and z = 2.5 were applied to the scatter plot, providing a visual guide for distinguishing between peripheral nodes, non-hub connector nodes, non-hub kinless nodes, and connector hubs.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Insights or Next Steps\n",
        "*   Further analysis could involve identifying the specific nodes that fall into each role category and investigating their attributes or functions within the network to understand their particular significance.\n",
        "*   The identified node roles can inform strategies for network intervention, such as targeting connector hubs for efficient information spread or identifying peripheral nodes for community-specific optimizations.\n"
