        "- **Edge Addition:** Edges were added to `G` directly from the processed DataFrame `df`'s values using `G.add_edges_from(df.values.tolist())`. Since `nx.Graph()` was used, any potential multi-edges or self-loops in the raw data would have been implicitly handled by `networkx` (multi-edges would become single edges, self-loops would be ignored as `nx.Graph()` doesn't support them by default).\n"
